# GitHub credentials for private repositories.
#
# COMMITTED, and safe to be: neither the token nor its cache-isolation entropy
# is in this file. Both name environment variables, so every user of this repo
# supplies their own and no two of them share a `secret-hash`.
#
# You do NOT need this for public repositories — `import_source` and
# `publish_source` reach those unauthenticated. Leave the variables unset and
# the secret is simply absent from the store (the client says so once, on
# stderr, and carries on).
#
# To use it, set both in the cloud environment's variables:
#   GITHUB_TOKEN               a PAT with access to the repos you want
#   CAOS_GITHUB_TOKEN_ENTROPY  any random string of 16+ chars, yours alone
#
# MIND THE FIRST ONE IN A CLOUD SESSION: the container ALREADY has a
# `GITHUB_TOKEN`, set by the harness for its own clone (measured — a session
# with neither variable set warned about the ENTROPY, which is only reached
# once the value has resolved). So setting only the entropy here silently
# promotes the harness's token into a caos secret. That may be exactly what you
# want; decide it deliberately, and name a variable of your own
# (`value:env=MY_GITHUB_PAT`) if it is not.
#
# Requiring BOTH is what makes that a choice rather than an accident: an
# ambient token with no entropy would otherwise have run with no cache
# isolation at all.
#
# The entropy is what keeps your cached results out of anyone else's reach: it
# is a bearer capability for the cache, so it must not be shared and must not
# be committed. That is why `entropy:env=` is required here rather than the
# literal `entropy=` that `caos secrets` writes for a local store.
name=github-token
value:env=GITHUB_TOKEN
entropy:env=CAOS_GITHUB_TOKEN_ENTROPY

# WHO MAY READ IT. A reader is a path in THIS tree, eval-path'd — which is why
# the caos-std mount has to exist: `caos-std/llm-step` resolves through the
# root .caos-expr above. A reader naming a path the tree does not carry grants
# nothing and is dropped with a warning, so if imports of private repos fail
# with a permission error, check this path first.
reader=caos-std/llm-step
